<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- Token chain -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="pa-card">
    <div class="pa-card__header">
        <div class="pa-card__title">
            <h3 class="pa-card__title-text">How the tokens re-skin</h3>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pa-card__body">
        <p>Most icons trace through a shared, cross-ecosystem contract, so a single
            override re-skins Pure Admin, the pure-css shell and the KeenMate web
            components together:</p>
        <pre class="pa-code">.pa-icon--search  →  var(--pa-icon-src)
                  →  var(--pa-icon-search)
                  →  var(--base-icon-search, <em>inline Lucide fallback</em>)</pre>
        <ul>
            <li><strong><code>--base-icon-*</code></strong> — the shared contract
                (published in <code>@keenmate/base-css-variables</code> and
                mirrored by <code>@keenmate/pure-css</code>). Override once to
                re-skin everything.</li>
            <li><strong><code>--pa-icon-*</code></strong> — Pure Admin's family;
                falls back to an inline Lucide glyph so icons always render even
                without the contract loaded.</li>
            <li><strong>pa-only glyphs</strong> — a few (e.g.
                <code>--pa-icon-favorites</code>) are Pure Admin-only and are
                <em>not</em> part of the <code>--base-*</code> contract, so they're
                defined directly with no <code>--base-icon-*</code> route.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>To retarget a single glyph, set its <code>--pa-icon-<em>name</em></code>
            (or the shared <code>--base-icon-<em>name</em></code>) at
            <code>:root</code> or on any subtree.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- C2: hover-to-fill -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="pa-card">
    <div class="pa-card__header">
        <div class="pa-card__title">
            <h3 class="pa-card__title-text">Hover-to-fill (enabled buttons &amp; tabs)</h3>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pa-card__body">
        <p>An icon can swap to a <strong>filled</strong> variant when its enabled
            button or tab is hovered. It's opt-in on two axes:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Per glyph</strong> — an icon opts in by declaring a filled
                source on <code>--pa-icon-src-hover</code>. Icons without one are
                left untouched.</li>
            <li><strong>Per context</strong> — the swap only fires inside an
                <em>enabled</em> <code>.pa-btn</code> or <code>.pa-tabs__item</code>
                on <code>:hover</code>. Disabled controls never react.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="pa-callout pa-callout--warning">
            <div class="pa-callout__icon"><span class="pa-icon pa-icon--warning" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
            <div class="pa-callout__content">
                <p class="pa-callout__title">The default Lucide set is outline-only</p>
                <p>Lucide ships no filled glyphs, so hover-to-fill is
                    <strong>dormant out of the box</strong> — the mechanism is
                    present but there's nothing to fill to. To activate it, point
                    <code>--pa-icon-src-hover</code> at a filled glyph from a set
                    that has one — <strong>Tabler</strong> (a Lucide look-alike),
                    Fluent, or Material. The live demo below uses a Tabler
                    regular/filled bell pair.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <h4 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Live demo</h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted">Hover each control. The first uses a
            Tabler outline→filled bell and morphs; the second is the Lucide bell and
            stays outline (nothing to fill to); the third is the <em>same</em>
            Tabler bell but disabled, so it never reacts despite being fillable
            (proving the disabled gate). No transition —
            <code>mask-image</code> can't tween, so the fill is an instant swap.</p>
        <div class="component-showcase" style="gap: 1rem; align-items: center;">
            <button class="pa-btn pa-btn--primary">
                <span class="pa-icon demo-fill-bell" aria-hidden="true"></span> Subscribe (Tabler)
            </button>
            <button class="pa-btn pa-btn--secondary">
                <span class="pa-icon pa-icon--bell" aria-hidden="true"></span> Subscribe (Lucide)
            </button>
            <button class="pa-btn pa-btn--primary" disabled>
                <span class="pa-icon demo-fill-bell" aria-hidden="true"></span> Disabled (Tabler)
            </button>
        </div>

        <div class="pa-tabs pa-tabs--full" style="margin-top: 1.5rem; max-width: 32rem;">
            <button class="pa-tabs__item pa-tabs__item--active">
                <span class="pa-icon demo-fill-bell" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span>Notifications</span>
            </button>
            <button class="pa-tabs__item">
                <span class="pa-icon pa-icon--user" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span>Profile</span>
            </button>
        </div>

        <h4 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">How to enable it</h4>
        <p>Define a modifier that declares both a resting (outline) and a hover
            (filled) source. The framework's global rule swaps them on hover:</p>
        <pre class="pa-code">/* your glyph — resting outline + filled-on-hover source */
.pa-icon--bell {
  --pa-icon-src:       var(--pa-icon-bell);        /* Lucide outline */
  --pa-icon-src-hover: url("…tabler filled bell…"); /* filled variant */
}

/* framework rule (ships in core) — no-op unless a glyph declared a hover src.
   Sets mask-image directly (not --pa-icon-src) so the var(--pa-icon-src)
   fallback isn't self-referential — a custom-property cycle would blank the
   mask and leave a solid box. */
.pa-btn:not(:disabled):hover .pa-icon,
.pa-tabs__item:not(:disabled):hover .pa-icon {
  mask-image: var(--pa-icon-src-hover, var(--pa-icon-src));
}</pre>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted">The fallback to
            <code>--pa-icon-src</code> is what makes the rule safe to ship
            globally: any icon that didn't declare a filled source simply keeps its
            resting glyph.</p>
    </div>
</div>
